      ],
      "application_cycle": "rolling",
      "next_deadline": "Request a TEFRA hearing through HWS at least six weeks before the CDLAC application; no County fee was stated in the Board file.",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "false",
      "layering_notes": "Riverside County's Housing and Workforce Solutions (HWS) department runs the Urban County HUD programs, PLHA, HHAP, Homekey+ sponsorships and project loans, while the Housing Authority of the County of Riverside (HACR, same Board sitting as Commissioners) supplies project-based vouchers, housing successor funds and land; rivcohws.org and harivco.org block automated access, so records were built from Board of Supervisors files on riversidecountyca.iqm2.com and media.rivcocob.org, RUHS Behavioral Health, the Assessor and the County Housing Element. HACR does not issue multifamily bonds; CMFA and CSCDA are the usual issuers with the County or the host city holding the TEFRA hearing. Source is the February 4, 2025 Board item on media.rivcocob.org.",
      "source_url": "https://media.rivcocob.org/proceeds/2025/p2025_02_04_files/21.01001.pdf",
